post.description:
A company needs its owner's verified email, as the welcome credits come once per email. A
person's first company, which gets them, needs them to show they're a person, on the site;
through the assistant or an AI app (no browser) it can't be asked.

Only the invited, verified email can start, so a forwarded link is useless to anyone else;
a guest invite, only its guest (its link signs them in). A first start takes the candidate's
pledge to answer on their own.

get.description:
Shown to anyone with the link, signed in or not, before they start. Signed in with a
verified email, it also says how far they got, so a finished test is never offered again;
an unverified one could claim anyone's address, so it learns nothing about that person.

post.description:
Sends the invite again, as an owner or admin does on the candidate's page: refused for a
candidate who finished (409) or one prepza doesn't email (invited without a sign-in, 409);
the invite keeps its return address and theme.
